C03: a folder reaches the private trash across volumes (FILES1605)

FILES1603 measured that the deletion reader and the known-file adapter find the named folder, but Directory.Move refuses another volume and the redirected Desktop (D:) and the product's private trash (under the profile on C:) sit on different drives. `MoveDirectory` keeps Directory.Move on the same root and otherwise recreates the tree in the private trash, copies every file, verifies that as many entries arrived as left, and only then removes the source; the receipt and the post-read are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


